# arvo-sparse, backlog

> **Type-surface reminder**: new entries use `arvo::USize` /
> `Bool` / `UFixed<N, 0, S>` instead of `usize` / `bool` / `u*`;
> `notko::Maybe` / `Outcome` instead of `Option` / `Result`. See
> `rules/type-surface.md`.

Round 202605031748 (#313) collapsed the BitMatrix family onto
`BitMatrix<W, const N: Cap>` chassis. Algorithms ship today against
`W = Bits<64, Hot, Unsigned>` for up to 64-node adjacency.
Instantiating the same algorithms with `W = Bits<256, Hot,
Unsigned>` extends to 256 nodes without an algorithmic-shape change.

## Wider-W ergonomic helpers

`rcm_reorder`, `block_diagonal`, `dulmage_mendelsohn` accept the
chassis form. The 256-wide instantiation extends the algorithms to
larger sparse adjacencies via arvo's MultiContainer
plumbing. Promote when a concrete consumer surfaces >64-node
adjacency; cookbook documentation of the wider-W pattern is the only
deferred work.

## SpMV

Sparse matrix-vector multiply patterns. Deferred per the original
design (T3 decisions #71-74). Same representation and API
surface as the above algorithms; add when a concrete consumer need
surfaces.
